The same story appears in the Skandapurāṇa (Brahmakhaṇḍa—Setu-mādhava 29) in a slightly different, but in a more detailed form. Here, the birds are actually devarṣis (sages from among the gods). रैक्व was so great that he had made all the sacred rivers stay in his hermitage as three small lakes. When जानश्रुति approached him for spiritual wisdom, he was asked to bathe in these lakes first. Then, his मिन्द् became quiet and fit enough to receive the teaching. When रैक्व taught him spiritual wisdom, he attained लिबेरतिओन्.
See also RAIKVA.
